  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 7♠. Souths wins the ♥A and appears to have no losers. He should try to draw trump immediately so that the defenders do not get any ruffs.\n\nSouth cashes dummy's ♠A and ♠K and must get back to the closed hand to draw the last trump. There is some danger in trying to return to the South hand with the ♣A. As East and West have only 3 clubs between them, it is not unlikely that one of them will be void. If the player with a club void has a trump left, the grand slam will be defeated.\n\nSouth should try to reenter his hand by trumping one of North's diamond winners. After cashing a top diamond, South can afford to ruff the second diamond with the ♠Q or ♠J as long as trumps are 3-2. South uses his remaining trump honour to draw the last trump and takes the balance of the tricks.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥K against 7♠. Souths wins the ♥A and appears to have no losers. He should try to draw trump immediately so that the defenders do not get any ruffs.",
    "South cashes dummy's ♠A and ♠K and must get back to the closed hand to draw the last trump. There is some danger in trying to return to the South hand with the ♣A. As East and West have only 3 clubs between them, it is not unlikely that one of them will be void. If the player with a club void has a trump left, the grand slam will be defeated.",
    "South should try to reenter his hand by trumping one of North's diamond winners. After cashing a top diamond, South can afford to ruff the second diamond with the ♠Q or ♠J as long as trumps are 3-2. South uses his remaining trump honour to draw the last trump and takes the balance of the tricks."
  ],
